{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3177","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3177","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3177\",\"parent_revision\":\"f4d5aa700a7e8d21d1fb7e1e5ee599d77d367e46451216aab2a444e813dc5325\",\"root_revision\":\"f4d5aa700a7e8d21d1fb7e1e5ee599d77d367e46451216aab2a444e813dc5325\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nFour function-local imports carrying `# ruff: ignore[import-outside-top-level]` remain in the plugin. Each is a workaround for a real import cycle rather than a fix for one.\\n\\nLocations observed 2026-08-23 after the parsing.py/entry_blocks.py cycle was fixed:\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` (two occurrences around line 1473-1475, deferring `pathlib.Path` and `ruamel.yaml.YAML`)\\n- `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py`\\n- `backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py`\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py` around line 1389\\n\\nWhy this matters rather than being cosmetic: this repo's rules prohibit suppressions as a mechanism (`.claude/rules/linting-exceptions.md`, `.claude/rules/astral-tool-overrides.md`), and a deferred import is a symptom of a module graph problem, not a solution to one. The suppression makes the cycle invisible to the linter that would otherwise keep pointing at it, so it persists indefinitely and attracts new deferred imports \u2014 that is exactly what happened in parsing.py, which accumulated three of them before the cycle was broken.\\n\\nEvidence that the fix is tractable: the parsing.py/entry_blocks.py cycle turned out to hinge on a single symbol (`now_iso`), and extracting it into a `backlog_core/timestamps.py` leaf module removed both deferred imports and both suppressions with zero test-count change (3459 passed before and after). The same shape of analysis \u2014 identify the minimal set of symbols crossing the cycle, extract to a leaf module \u2014 is likely to apply to at least some of these four.\\n\\nImpact if left: the module graph keeps its cycles, the linter stays silenced on them, and each new cross-module need in these files adds another deferred import with another suppression.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the fix direction demonstrated on the parsing/entry_blocks cycle was to move the shared symbol into its own leaf module and import it at module scope from both sides, never to alias or defer around the collision. Whether that generalises to each of these four needs per-cycle analysis during grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Encountered while fixing the parsing/entry_blocks cycle during PR #3165, 2026-08-23\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"96e805c689074a29455893ebd849fb87d072ae7844378fbc8b0459d49aa43847\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQPWsrQ\"}"}